{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan reworked to remove both fixed 24-hour rollout waits without weakening the safety properties. A2-2 now stops/scrubs legacy writes while retaining max(sidecar, legacy) read compatibility and an old/new-writer self-healing oracle; rollout evidence is a descendant reconcile workflow plus explicit host-binary refresh and no-old-process proof. A6-1 now requires quiescence plus direct epoch-mismatch refusal from the descendant GHA build, deployed review-bot runtime, and explicitly refreshed host runtime; A6-0b records the deployment receipt and persistent-clone convergence. Epic, A2-2, A6-0b, and A6-1 descriptions updated. Dependency-first plan reviews will run only when each ticket becomes claimable; no force used."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785780479709366001,"uuid":"d603642e-4fe7-47bb-80da-2c107eeb80af"}